# Copy to .env (gitignored). Everything has a working default.

# HF_TOKEN=hf_...          # the model is PUBLIC - only needed behind a proxy

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE MEMORY KNOB
#
# 0.80 of 121 GiB unified is ~97 GiB claimed. NVIDIA's own guidance for this
# model is 0.91; the published DGX Spark run used 0.80 and reported ~75 GB of
# KV cache with ~12 GB of system memory left over. On unified memory that
# remainder is not headroom you can spend - it holds the page cache, your shell
# and any desktop session - which is why the lower number is the default here.
#
# vLLM sizes KV from NVML, and NVML reports NO FRAMEBUFFER on GB10, so it is
# profiling against a pool the OS also lives in. Same reason
# vllm_gpu_memory_utilization defaults to 0.85 elsewhere in this repo.
# GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.80

# 262144, not the checkpoint's 1,048,576. A 1M window is real on this model -
# only 6 of its 52 layers pay a per-token K/V cost - but vLLM's pool arithmetic
# is not SGLang's, and the published DGX Spark run reduced this for KV headroom.
# Raise it and re-measure with ws up vllm-bench-serve; do not assume.
# MAX_MODEL_LEN=262144

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SPECULATIVE DECODING - dspark | dflash | mtp | none
#
# Measured on a DGX Spark (code generation, single stream / 8 concurrent):
#
#   none     81.3 / 241.7 tok/s     the THROUGHPUT-optimal choice
#   dflash   95.5 / 268.6 tok/s     +17% / +11%
#   mtp     111.4 / 302.3 tok/s     +37% / +25%   no second checkpoint
#   dspark  124.2 / 354.6 tok/s     +53% / +47%   <- default, wins on both axes
#
# SPEC_METHOD=dspark

# The published comparison ran `mtp` with `moe_backend triton` rather than
# marlin. Recorded, not adopted: it is one line in one article with no stated
# reason, and MOE_BACKEND is the flag that decides whether the experts load
# quantised at all. If mtp misbehaves here, try MOE_BACKEND=triton first.

# 3, NOT 7. Measured on this class of box, depth 3 beats depth 7 for
# single-stream use. This repo has already been bitten by inheriting a `k` from
# a model card (decisions.md#dspark-1m-recipe) - if you change it, prove it:
#   ws up spec-decode-accept        before and after
# SPEC_TOKENS=3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE TWO FLAGS WITH NO EQUIVALENT ELSEWHERE IN THIS REPO
#
# marlin, because on GB10 the NVFP4 path is a W4A16 Marlin kernel - native FP4
# tensor-core execution is GB200. The model card's own hardware table says so.
# Changing this to a native-FP4 backend does not make it faster here; it makes
# it not load.
# MOE_BACKEND=marlin

# The hybrid mamba state is a fixed allocation. `align` is what the published
# DGX Spark run used.
# MAMBA_BACKEND=flashinfer
# MAMBA_CACHE_MODE=align

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `nemotron_v3` here, `nemotron_3` in SGLang. Neither is a typo. Copying one
# into the other fails at startup, which is the GOOD outcome.
# REASONING_PARSER=nemotron_v3
# TOOL_CALL_PARSER=qwen3_coder

# Weights. Public, OpenMDW-1.1.
# MODEL=nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Lightning-30B-A3B-NVFP4
# DSPARK_DRAFT=nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Lightning-30B-A3B-NVFP4-DSpark
# DFLASH_DRAFT=nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Lightning-30B-A3B-NVFP4-DFlash
# SERVED_NAME=nemotron-3.5-lightning

# SERVED_NAME is not a repo id, so a tokenizer cannot be loaded from it.
# vllm-bench-serve needs TOKENIZER set to the HF id or it dies minutes in.

# A release tag, not a nightly - NVFP4 + DSpark for this checkpoint is in 0.27.x.
# VLLM_IMAGE=vllm/vllm-openai:v0.27.1

# 8895, so it does not collide with the other serving workspaces.
# PORT=8895
